WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.240
I've never been much for smoking

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.900
But taking a bullet to your chest

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.820
Will make you a lot less worried

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:08.220
About the slow deaths of the world

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:11.580
Long story short I took a job I shouldn't have

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:14.800
They say the pretty ones will always get you killed

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.560
But he was so damn handsome I couldn't resist

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.120
I was a frog in a slow pot of boiling water

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.700
I was the first clown to get into the clown car

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.080
You don't know to get out until it's too late

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.340
One thing led to another

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.860
And I found myself slow dancing with the devil in the moonlight

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:38.200
Except instead of leaving room for Jesus,

00:00:38.380 --> 00:00:42.020
He left room for a 357 magnum

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.260
I won't bore you with the details

00:00:45.380 --> 00:00:48.140
So I'll cut right to the quick

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:51.480
A lot of people died because of this man

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.540
William J. Barnum

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:57.760
a.k.a. The Colonel

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:01.300
Just like the clown at my bar mitzvah

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:05.980
I knew he was trouble from the moment I laid eyes on him

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.060
And just like Bozo The Magnificent

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.300
A lot of people died when he walked into my life

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:15.640
*Mark giggling*

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:17.920
A lot of people died when he wa—

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:18.800
*clears throat*

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:22.180
I've been chasing him down ever since

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:27.740
We were like two naked men running on the same treadmill.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.340
Uncomfortably close

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.900
But always just a step behind

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.980
But no one can run forever

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:40.920
Especially not with 200 pounds of sweaty detective breathing down your neck

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:43.380
It hasn't been easy though

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:47.380
I can't count how many countries I've cornered him in

00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:52.800
Couldn't tell you how many times I've had him in my big, strong hands

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.080
Every time I think I've got him for good

00:01:57.420 --> 00:02:00.940
He somehow manages to slip away

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.860
But he's running out of holes to hide in

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:09.060
I mean that literally, metaphorically, and euphemistically

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.380
It doesn't matter how crafty you think you are

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:16.140
If you've been on the run for years and years

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:17.660
Eventually

00:02:17.980 --> 00:02:20.540
You're gonna make a mistake

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.320
Word of advice:

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.660
If you're running away from your problems, never become to attached to anything

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:32.500
Families, lovers, briefcases on top of your car.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.320
Some things are best left behind

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:39.180
The Colonel is a slippery one

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:45.120
Shedding names as easily as a snake sheds a few pounds before bikini season

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:50.400
He's going through pseudonym after pseudonym trying to cover his tracks

00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:56.660
But he always manages to fall back into the same familiar ways

00:02:56.980 --> 00:03:02.100
Drinking, fighting, flirting

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.760
Dancing

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:08.740
SUBSCRIBE TO MARKIPLIER!

